      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "Let $w(y)$ be a weight for node $y,$ where $y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}.$ We want to write the selected node $\\overset{^}{y}$ as \"the value of $y$ that makes $w(y)$ as large as possible.\"\n\nWhich of the following correctly defines $\\overset{^}{y}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We want $\\overset{^}{y}$ to be an *input value* $y$ where the weight $w(y)$ is as large as possible. \n\nThat is exactly what $\\operatorname{arg}⁡max$ returns.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}}w(y).\n$$",
